//
// WHAT IT ADDS TO A FRAME. The renderer draws the opaque meshes in one render pass.
// With extended materials in the frame it draws them in up to three:
//   1. the opaque meshes that do not read the frame, the sky not yet;
//   2. [a capture of 1] the opaque meshes that reflect the frame ('reflections'
//      above 0: screen-space reflections), which see everything the first pass drew;
//   3. [the sky; a capture of 1 and 2 and the sky] the glass, which refracts what
//      the capture shows behind it, and then the rest of the see-through meshes.
// A capture is the colour target copied into level 0 of a pyramid (a texture of
// several levels, each filtered down from the one above, capture.slang), and
