// it costs a pass a level and is made only when something reads it. This is the
// "scene colour" and "opaque texture" capture other engines make before their
// transparent pass (Unity's _CameraOpaqueTexture, Unreal's SceneColor copy,
// Godot's screen texture), and the reflecting meshes are drawn after it as
// Frostbite's and Unity's forward SSR do. What it cannot do is stated with the
