// Views, planar mirrors and reflective water, and reflection probes.
//
// A VIEW is the scene drawn from another camera into a texture of its own:
// a size, a layer mask (which of the draw list's items it draws), and a
// colour texture, held by the renderer under a TextureHandle, that any
// material can sample (a custom pipeline's, or ViewMaterials' below).
// A security-camera screen, a minimap, a portal's opening and a mirror are
// all that: a view, and a material that shows it. The view is drawn into
// its own texture, in its own submission, before the frame's main render
// (a view drawn at the start of the frame, as the draw lists of its
// camera say). Render the views before creating the encoder the main
// 'render' records into, in the order that a view is drawn after the views
// whose pictures its scene shows.
//
// Why a submission each. The frame's uniforms, the instances and the bones
// are one set of buffers, written by 'queue.writeBuffer', which the GPU
// runs after everything submitted before it: so each camera's pass is
// recorded and submitted before the next camera's writes, and one set of
// buffers serves every view. (The alternative, a set of buffers a view, is
// more to keep and buys nothing a submission does not.)
//
// Layers. A DrawItem is on layers (a bit each; 'DrawList.setLayers'); a
// view draws the items its layer mask meets, so a screen is left out of
// the picture of the camera that feeds it, and a mirror out of its own
// reflection.
//
// NESTING. A view that shows another view's picture (a monitor, in a room a
// camera films, that shows another camera) is drawn after that view; its
// 'nest' is how many views deep it sits (0: it shows none), and 'render'
// draws it only if that is no more than 'maxNest' (default 1: a view within a
// view). A view deeper than that is not drawn that frame, and shows what it
// last held, so the recursion is cut at a depth the program chooses and
// costs what it says. A view never draws its own screen: put the screen on a
// layer the view's mask leaves out, and the picture inside the picture is
// last frame's, one frame behind, not a second pass.
//
// FOG. A view can have the volumetric fog of fog.cone over its picture, so that a
// mirror or a portal shows the air the main view does: 'enableFog' makes the view's
// own passes and volume (the size of its picture), and the view's 'fog' settings, read
// every picture, say what the air is and whether it is drawn ('fog.enabled'). The
// fog is recorded into the picture's own submission, after the scene, over the picture's
// depth (which 'render' keeps for it), and reads the cascades and the shadow parameters
// the picture's own render has just written for its camera. The camera's eye is its
// position (a reflected camera's reflection) and its distances are planar, so the fog of
// a mirror's picture is the plain fog of the camera at the reflected eye.
//
// PLANAR MIRRORS and WATER. The camera that sees in a mirror is
// 'camera.reflectedAbout(plane)' (camera.cone): the world reflected about
// the plane before the camera sees it, the near plane replaced by the mirror
// plane itself (Lengyel's oblique clip) so nothing behind the mirror is
// drawn, and the clip space's x flipped so the triangles keep their winding.
// Its view, the size of the frame, is the reflection; ViewMaterials'
// mirror material reads it at the fragment's own screen position, with a
// Fresnel blend with a body colour and a scrolling normal map's offset for
// water (viewmat.slang).
//
// REFLECTION PROBES. A cube map captured at a point (six right-handed
// 90 degree cameras, 256 texels a face), filtered the way the sky is: the
// environment's own pipelines (ibl.slang), its mip chain by box filtering,
// a specular cube by GGX importance sampling at 6 roughness steps, a
// diffuse cube. A physically based copy whose model's origin lies inside the
// probe's box is lit by the probe's cubes in place of the sky's, and its
// reflection vector is box-projected (pbr.slang, 'probeDirection') so the
// reflection of a room's walls sits where the walls are. The probe's cubes
// belong to the 'ReflectionProbe' value the program keeps; the renderer holds only the
// group the shaders read. Probes need a renderer drawing into RGBA16_FLOAT.

// The mask of every layer
pub const LAYERS_ALL = 0xffffffffu32;

// How many views deep a view may be drawn, by default
pub const DEFAULT_MAX_NEST = 1u32;

